  "$comment": "Opposing UI action pairs checked by scripts/vision-pairs-check.mjs. Each member's fill and the shared background are a DDD or HAX UI token name (resolved from elements/d-d-d/lib for light and dark), a literal hex, or the word background for an unfilled (outlined / text) button. cues lists what tells the pair apart besides color: outline, pattern, label, strike, position (a switch knob), weight (bold type); icon is recorded but not counted, since a 16px glyph is not readable at a glance. See haxtheweb/issues for the color vision tracking issue. evidence lists source snippets that must still exist for a declared non-color cue to count (file + text), so removing a hatch or underline later turns the pair into a fail instead of a silent cue.",
